  "stem": "In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graphs of \\(y = 3x - 4\\) and \\(y = -2x + 16\\) intersect at the point \\((a, b)\\). What is the value of \\(a + b\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "12"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "At the intersection, \\(3x - 4 = -2x + 16\\), so \\(5x = 20\\) and \\(x = 4\\).",
    "Then \\(y = 3(4) - 4 = 8\\), so \\((a, b) = (4, 8)\\) and \\(a + b = 12\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "x, y = symbols('x y')\nsol = solve([y - (3*x - 4), y - (-2*x + 16)], [x, y])\nassert sol == {x: 4, y: 8}\nassert [Rational(s) for s in spr_answers] == [sol[x] + sol[y]]",
